; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Archimedes' Spiral
; CATEGORY: Spirals & Curves
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     archimedean spiral, polar coordinates, setxy, measurement
; SUMMARY:  Plots the spiral where the distance from the center grows evenly with the angle, and measures its equal gaps.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   In Archimedes' spiral, every time the angle grows by one degree
;   the distance from the center grows by the same small amount. So
;   the gap between one turn and the next is always the same, like
;   the groove on a record or a rolled-up carpet. The program draws
;   two interleaved arms in two colors, then a ruler line from the
;   center with a dot wherever it crosses the spiral, so you can
;   see the dots are evenly spaced.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change GROWTH (steps per degree) or TURNS.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * polar coordinates: an angle and a distance give a point
;   * x = r sin(angle) and y = r cos(angle) in turtle directions
;   * the formula r = growth x angle
;   * checking a property of a curve by measuring it
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Use three arms, 120 degrees apart.
;   * Change the formula to r = growth x angle x angle / 1000. Are the
;     gaps still equal?
;   * Make r shrink instead, so the spiral winds inwards.
; ============================================================

make "growth 0.12
make "turns 6

; Plot the spiral, starting at angle :start.
to archimedes :start :color
  setpencolor :color
  penup
  for [a 0 360 * :turns 3] [
    localmake "r :growth * :a
    setxy :r * sin :a + :start :r * cos :a + :start
    pendown
  ]
end

; A ruler from the center along heading :h, with a black dot where
; each arm crosses it. The first arm crosses at angles h, h + 360, ...
; so at distances growth x h, growth x (h + 360), ... The second arm
; is 180 degrees behind.
to ruler :h
  setpencolor [40 40 40] setpensize 2
  penup home setheading :h pendown
  forward :growth * 360 * :turns
  setpensize 10
  for [k 0 :turns - 1] [
    foreach [0 180] [
      localmake "r :growth * (:h - ? + 360 * :k)
      if :r > 0 [
        penup home setheading :h forward :r
        dot pos
      ]
    ]
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [250 248 242]
setpensize 3
archimedes 0 [220 60 60]
archimedes 180 [40 110 200]
ruler 300
penup setxy -390 -285 setpencolor [90 90 90]
label [Every gap between the arms is the same: 180 x growth steps]
